# Clarity

A person should know where they are, what they can do, and what happens next without hovering.

- Navigation shows words. Icon-only is reserved for a row action that also has a tooltip on wide layouts (delete, close).
- One filled button per screen. Everything else is text or outline. The label is a verb plus a noun: `New task`, not `+` or `Create`.
- Page title is the object (`Board name`, `Workspaces`). At most one short subtitle. No slogans in the product shell.
- A task row shows the title, then status (`To do` / `Doing` / `Done`). Priority only when it is not medium. Assignee only when set. Tap the row to edit.
- Empty state is one sentence plus the same primary button. Do not add a second call to action.
- Hide controls that do nothing. Do not show a disabled social login or an empty `onTap`.
- Group board tools (members, AI, board settings) behind one labeled menu. They are not peers of New task.
- Confirm destructive actions by naming the object: `Delete "Sprint board"?`. Use `AppColors.error` for the confirm button only.
- Errors are a sentence from `ApiError.userMessage` or l10n, plus Retry when the call can be repeated. Never `error.toString()`.
- Strings go in both `app_en.arb` and `app_vi.arb`.

```dart
// ❌ IconButton(icon: Icon(Icons.add))
// ✅ AppButton(label: l10n.newTask, onPressed: onCreate)
```
